      "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants an incident retrospective for a production API outage caused by a bad cache invalidation rule. Let me think about what makes a good incident retrospective and structure it well.\n\nKey sections requested:\n1. Impact\n2. Timeline\n3. Contributing factors\n4. Detection gaps\n5. Remediation\n6. Prevention work\n7. Owner handoff\n\nLet me write this in practical language for engineers and managers. Target 450-550 words.\n\nLet me draft this. I want it to be realistic and specific. A bad cache invalidation rule - this is a common real-world scenario. Let me think about what happens:\n\n- A cache invalidation rule change causes stale data to be served\n- This could cause incorrect responses, cascading failures, etc.\n\nLet me create a realistic scenario. Something like: a change to the cache key generation or TTL logic caused cache entries to never expire, or caused incorrect cache keys, leading to serving stale data or cache poisoning.\n\nLet me write a concise but complete retrospective.\n\nI'll aim for a clean structure with headers. Let me count words roughly as I go.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n---\n\n**Incident Retrospective: Production API Outage \u2014 Cache Invalidation Failure**\n\n**Incident ID:** INC-2024-0317\n**Severity:** SEV-1\n**Duration:** 2h 14m\n**Date:** [Date]\n\n**Summary**\nA change to the cache invalidation rule for the user-profile service caused the API to serve stale profile data for ~2 hours, degrading read performance and returning incorrect values for a subset of requests.\n\n**Impact**\n- API p99 latency rose from 120ms to 1.8s.\n- ~18% of profile reads returned cached data from up to 45 minutes prior.\n- ~3,200 support tickets and 400 refund requests tied to incorrect balances shown.\n- No data loss; no security impact.\n- Peak error rate: 6.4% (5xx from cache backend timeouts).\n\n**Timeline**\n- 14:02 \u2014 Deploy of PR #4471 (cache key TTL refactor) merged to main.\n- 14:05 \u2014 Auto-deploy to production.\n- 14:11 \u2014 First elevated latency alerts; on",
      "text_preview": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants an incident retrospective for a production API outage caused by a bad cache invalidation rule. Let me think about what makes a good incident retrospective and structure it well.\n\nKey sections requested:\n1. Impact\n2. Timeline\n3. Contributing factors\n4. Detection gaps\n5. Remediation\n6. Prevention",
